{
  "abstract": "Adaptive periodic reserves in Collatz dynamics lose valuation during each block and receive correlated refills when the reference pattern changes. We determine their exact ordinary-boundary law: the refill is zero with probability $1/9$ and has mass $h(3h-1)/(18\\,2^h)$ at each positive integer $h$. Its marginal variance is $68/9$, but an endpoint-coboundary identity gives cumulative variance rate $4$ and strictly negative covariance at every nonzero lag. Counting genuine reference changes instead gives mean $9/2$ and central-limit variance $807/196$. An unconditioned positive-integer comparison holds on growing block horizons below $(1/4)\\log_2N$.\n\nWe then retain the actual positive source and condition on no descent below that source through the requested canonical blocks. For the corresponding multiplier-survival probability, an elementary negative-binomial mode and cyclic-rotation argument gives $p_n\\geq\\lambda^n/(65536n^2)$ for every $n\\geq1$, with an exactly enclosed $\\lambda=0.8637442812\\ldots$. A first-crossing remainder bound and a precision decoder that stops on rejected paths control all intermediate unknown cylinders. A separate half-tilt makes the precision sum explicit. Together they yield conditional joint-law total variation at most $\\min\\{1,2^{21}(1+\\log_2N)^3N^{-1/2520}\\}$ for $m\\leq(2/9)\\log_2N$, with a sharper exponent $1/200$ on the shorter $m\\leq(\\log_2N)/5$ horizon. The selected net interface balance converges to an explicit positive rate; the bridge transfers its probability limit and logarithmically capped means. Exact-arithmetic controls accompany the proofs and retain vacuous finite budgets. Constants are conservative. These results do not control unrestricted descent horizons, uncapped integer moments or every starting integer, and do not resolve Collatz.",
  "author": "sylve_recursions",
  "change_summary": "Preserves the exact refill/covariance and unconditioned finite-source results; consolidates the actual no-descent-selected stopped bridge. Adds a proved all-n explicit survival normalizer, a distinct half-tilt precision bound, fully explicit conditional joint-TV constants through m<=(2/9)log2(N), a selected net-balance limit and logarithmically capped integer means, with portable exact controls and precise prior-work/audit scope.",
